> Quick checklist:
> (which I admit you may not need, and may be below your computer
> literacy level)
>
> How to compile nethack on Windows XP
>
> Get the Source from http://nethack.org/. Choose the one that ends in
> .tgz and save it in C:\nethack\source.
>
> Get 7-zip from http://www.7-zip.org and install it
> Get MinGW from http://www.mingw.org/download.shtml (you want the file
> MinGW3.1.0-1.exe) and install it in the default directory (c:/Program
> Files/MinGW)
>
> Unzip the source -
> Open the directory that you have the source (nethack-343-src.tgz) in
> and right click.
> Highlight 7-zip and then choose extract here
> A new file called nethack-343-src.tar will appear.
> Do the same thing again to this new file - right click, 7-zip-
> extract here.
> This will make a new folder (nethack-3.4.3) that will have a bunch of
> folders in it.
>
> Open that folder and open the /sys folder
> Open the /winnt folder
> Double click on the file nhsetup.bat
> A small window will appear for a couple seconds. This is nethack making
> some new folders and files specifically for Windows XP
>
> Right click on the file named Makefile.gcc
> Choose open with... and choose Wordpad.
> When the file opens, scroll down until you see the line
>
> #GRAPHICAL = Y
>
> and remove the # sign so the line is just
>
> GRAPHICAL =Y
>
> Save the file (left click on file and choose save) and close it.
>
> Now exit the folder your in (\sys\winnt) and go to the \src folder.
> Right click on an empty space of the window and highlight New and then
> select Text Document. It will make a new file and highlight the name so
> you can choose what you want to name it. Name the new file Install.bat
>
> Windows will bring up a warning asking if you want to change the file
> extension. Click yes.
>
>  Now, right click on the new file you just made (Install.bat) and
> choose edit
>
> Type these two lines:
>
> path= C:\Program Files\MinGW\bin
> mingw32-make -f Makefile.gcc install
>
> and then save the file.
>
> Close the file and with the /src window open, put the mouse pointer on
> top of make.bat
> and double-click it.
>
> A small window will open and a bunch of lines will scroll up it as the
> program compiles.
>
> Congratulations - you've done it. (Hopefully.)
>
> The new nethack program will be in the \binary file off the main source
> directory.
> If you put the source in c:\game\nethack\source, then you're new
> nethackW.exe will be in C:\games\nethack\source\nethack-3.4.3\binary
>
> Oh yeah, this makes the windows version of nethack, which I assume you
> want, as the tty version runs in a teeny window (at least on my
> machine)
> 
> hope this helps...
